From: Sheepsticked <72666364+Sheepsticked@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sms reports: receive delivery reports as +CDS (upstream PR
 #75)

Upstream: https://github.com/IchthysMaranatha/asterisk-chan-quectel @ 3d45c7f072131296a7e3c1a4faf5bb18751dbd87
Purpose: SMS delivery reports never reach Asterisk from a Quectel EC25.
         With AT+CNMI=2,1,0,2,0 the modem keeps the report in its
         separate "SR" storage, while the driver reads it with AT+CMGR
         from "SM", finds nothing and says nothing. Every SMS sent with
         Report: 1 then ends as a type 2 report (no report within the
         validity) although it was delivered (applies on top of 0007).

This is upstream pull request #75 by vskiwi, "SMS delivery reports:
receive status reports via +CDS" (head e810ed6f6ca21e0445614239fa59a89ef9605085,
open when taken), whole: driver, sample configurations, README and
tests. Its hunks in at_command.c, at_response.h, dc_config.c and
dc_config.h were placed by hand because 0001, 0004 and 0006 moved
their context; the code is unchanged.

The initialization sends AT+CNMI=2,1,0,1,0, so the modem passes each
report at once as the two-line URC "+CDS: <length>" plus the PDU;
at_read hands both lines over as one response (rb_find_nth_crlf) and
at_response_cds() gives the report to the same smsdb matching, report
channel and QuectelReport event as the +CDSI path, now shared in
at_handle_status_report(). A PDU without an SMSC address (length
octet 00) is accepted. New shared setting smsreport = cds | cdsi
(default cds); a modem that answers ERROR to <ds>=1 continues with
<ds>=2 and a warning, so its SMS keeps working as before.

Aster adds RES_CDS to at_response_is_unsolicited() (0001), so a report
that arrives during a QuectelAtCommand is not returned as that
command's output.
